hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1440","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Katheer Al-Suri in Fustat told us, Shurayh bin Al-Numan told us, Fulayh, who is Ibn Sulayman, told us, on the authority of Damrah bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab asked me about The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it in the exit prayer on the two Eids, and I said: “He recited: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has been split, and by the Qur’an Al-Majid, Abu Bakr said: This narration was not narrated by anyone I know of other than Fulayh bin Sulaiman. It was narrated by Malik bin Anas and Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, and they said: Omar asked Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, he said: Abu Al-Azhar told us of its origin, He said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Falayh"
"1441","And in the news of Al-Numan bin Bashir and Samurah bin Jundub, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “recited: Glorify the name of your Most High Lord, and has it come to you?” Hadith of Al-Ghashiya” and this is part of the difference in what is permissible."
